    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. The audit line confirms the new identity in action: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and everything derived from it follows.\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- Split region derivation out into a new `getRegion()` \u2014 the region code from the postcode range (NSW/VIC/QLD), with the city-table fallback and `UNKNOWN` default. This is the `REGION` segment of the customer code.\n- Rewrote `getLocality()` to read the region segment back off the `customerCode` (everything before the first `-`), so the locality derivation now *moves to* the region-and-hash identity rather than being computed independently. Returns `UNKNOWN` until a code is assigned.\n- `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()` were already derived from `customerCode`, so they automatically pick up the new value (Luhn now runs over the hex/region digits).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced the sequence-based `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` + `letterPrefix3` with `customerCodeFor(owner)` = `owner.getRegion() + \"-\" + telephoneNameHash(...)`, where `telephoneNameHash` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. Sequence numbers are gone entirely.\n- Postcode validation now uses `owner.getRegion()` (it previously piggy-backed on `getLocality()`, which now depends on the not-yet-assigned code), preserving the existing city-region postcode range check.\n- The create audit record logs `customerCode`, so it now emits the region-hash identity unchanged.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` field descriptions/examples to match the new identity.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The one acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash`) asserts the `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}` format, which now passes.",
